WEBVTT

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:04.077
Hello, I am Sergey Morozov.

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:07.824
For four and a half years, the 3R Swiss Imaging Network

00:00:08.084 --> 00:00:11.383
has used AI in everyday radiology. Here's what we learned.

00:00:12.323 --> 00:00:15.671
When a computer starts thinking slower than we do, we replace it.

00:00:15.931 --> 00:00:19.464
So what about an AI whose answer arrives after the report is signed?

00:00:20.404 --> 00:00:24.866
At the 3R Swiss Imaging Network, we measured exactly that in routine work.

00:00:25.126 --> 00:00:26.993
Four and a half years, 20 centers,

00:00:27.253 --> 00:00:32.731
10 AI tools from seven vendors, about 389,000 AI-assisted exams.

00:00:33.671 --> 00:00:38.726
Everyone asks if AI is accurate. Few ask if it arrives in time. And

00:00:38.986 --> 00:00:40.436
actually used by radiologists.

00:00:41.726 --> 00:00:42.528
The design:

00:00:42.788 --> 00:00:49.293
three data sources, triangulated. The AI platform dashboard, 96,874 exams.

00:00:49.553 --> 00:00:56.458
The radiology information system, 20,909 reports with and without AI used.

00:00:56.718 --> 00:00:59.048
And 58 radiologists surveyed twice.

00:01:00.038 --> 00:01:05.695
Three clocks. Clock one, AI latency. 2.06 minutes, median.

00:01:05.955 --> 00:01:11.982
The algorithm needs about 0. 2. 72% is data routing. A sprinter

00:01:12.242 --> 00:01:13.090
stuck in traffic.

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:16.496
Clock two: Does the result arrive in time?

00:01:16.756 --> 00:01:22.323
80.6% arrive before the report is started. 7.2% arrive after it is signed.

00:01:22.583 --> 00:01:26.440
1,584 exams, a first of its kind to our knowledge.

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:29.939
Clock three: The radiologist report time.

00:01:30.199 --> 00:01:32.250
When the result is there in time, it pays.

00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:38.312
Reports 26% faster in trauma radiography, 18 in knee MRI, adjusted for the radiologist.

00:01:38.572 --> 00:01:43.217
Trauma radiography alone, an estimated 0.69 of a radiologist a year.

00:01:43.477 --> 00:01:47.563
That is roughly a three to one return on investment for the platform.

00:01:47.823 --> 00:01:49.180
Two to one after adjustment.

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:56.663
On top of the clocks, we asked the radiologists. 91% use AI and 66% use AI regularly.

00:01:56.923 --> 00:02:02.722
They rate their AI tools 7.28 out of 10. Yet perceived productivity stays at

00:02:02.982 --> 00:02:05.080
2.94 out of 5.

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:10.308
Economists call it the Jevons paradox. Saved time may turn into more cases.

00:02:11.248 --> 00:02:13.763
From this triangulation come the monitoring metrics.

00:02:14.023 --> 00:02:16.214
Three clocks per tool, every quarter.

00:02:16.474 --> 00:02:19.174
We also propose a standardized radiologist questionnaire.

00:02:19.434 --> 00:02:25.328
Push studies to AI on completion, put time to display targets in contracts with AI vendors and distributors.

00:02:26.268 --> 00:02:31.081
And then the paradox. Today, AI can't keep up with the radiologist. Fix that,

00:02:31.341 --> 00:02:35.245
and with rising volumes, the radiologist may not keep up with AI.

00:02:35.505 --> 00:02:38.251
Will we still be able to monitor what it does?

00:02:39.441 --> 00:02:42.884
So we must monitor it and prepare radiologists to work with it.

00:02:43.144 --> 00:02:48.761
AI should run like a Swiss train, on time, comfortable, and taking us exactly where we need to go.

00:02:50.151 --> 00:02:51.045
Right result,

00:02:51.305 --> 00:02:56.320
right moment. From the 3R Swiss Imaging Network in Journal of American College of Radiology.

00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:59.370
Questions? Write to the 3R research team.
